    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe three separate identity fields (`customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`) are unified into a single stored `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`).\n\n**New identity utility & assign step** (renamed from the old `customerCode` pair):\n- `OwnerMemberId.java` (was `OwnerCustomerCode`) \u2014 `of(...)` now builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region code, 2-digit fiscal year of the registration date, the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex `HASH8`, and a single Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Added `fiscalYearOf(...)` and rewrote `regionOf(...)` to read the leading-letter region back out of the separator-free format.\n- `AssignMemberId.java` (was `AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 collision handling now de-duplicates the **memberId** (appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026), keyed off `getMemberId()`.\n\n**Field removal / rewiring:**\n- `Owner` model: `customerCode` field \u2192 `memberId` (column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`); schema.sql updated across h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres (widened to `VARCHAR(32)`/`TEXT` to fit the longer format plus a dedup suffix).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`; added `memberId`; updated the `locality` description.\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings and their `toMembershipNumber`/`toCheckDigit` methods; `toFiscalYear` and `toLocality` (which feeds `ownerSegment`) now read from `memberId`; the `toOwner` ignore-list entry retargeted to `memberId`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated`: human line and structured event now carry `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns `getMemberId()`.\n- `owners.POST.yml`: `assignCustomerCode` step \u2192 `assignMemberId`; javadoc references in `ValidatePostcode`, `RejectCityAtCapacity`, `CityCapacity`, `FiscalYear` updated.\n\n## Test result\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes (1 run, 0 failures). The runtime audit line confirms the new format, e.g. `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.\n\nOne note: `FiscalYear.label(...)` is now unused (the `fiscalYear` field is derived from the `memberId` segment rather than recomputed from the date). I left it in place as a harmless public utility helper; say the word if you'd prefer it removed.",
